WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.895
Basak, Lapu-Lapu City.

00:00:02.055 --> 00:00:04.168
Five households, the same stories.

00:00:04.309 --> 00:00:06.495
A student revises until one in the morning;

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:08.805
the suspension was posted at ten forty at

00:00:08.655 --> 00:00:11.350
night, on a page the family does not follow.

00:00:11.418 --> 00:00:12.477
A mother says:

00:00:12.709 --> 00:00:14.295
ligo na mo karon.

00:00:14.164 --> 00:00:16.295
The water cut was announced the night before,

00:00:16.364 --> 00:00:18.368
so the drum gets filled and everyone showers

00:00:18.218 --> 00:00:18.695
early.

00:00:18.891 --> 00:00:21.005
Another family lost power and the pump in

00:00:20.855 --> 00:00:21.441
one night:

00:00:21.927 --> 00:00:24.914
spoiled food, no shower, a late start at work.

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:27.168
And a hot afternoon with nothing prepared.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:29.322
This is where the notices live.

00:00:29.425 --> 00:00:31.792
MECO, the power company, posts brownouts as

00:00:31.705 --> 00:00:32.425
images.

00:00:32.613 --> 00:00:36.183
MCWD, the water district, posts water cuts

00:00:36.095 --> 00:00:37.840
under a news tab on its own site.

00:00:38.228 --> 00:00:41.682
DepEd, the education department, posts memos

00:00:41.605 --> 00:00:43.381
as PDF downloads.

00:00:43.769 --> 00:00:46.167
PAGASA, the weather bureau, is a fourth site

00:00:46.049 --> 00:00:47.244
in a fourth format.

00:00:47.491 --> 00:00:48.928
Two facts make this worse.

00:00:49.317 --> 00:00:51.092
Since the Department of Education's Order

00:00:51.005 --> 00:00:54.216
22 of 2024, brownout and heat suspensions

00:00:54.108 --> 00:00:56.591
are the mayor's call, so the post comes late.

00:00:56.779 --> 00:00:58.354
And power and water are coupled:

00:00:58.542 --> 00:01:00.486
when the grid drops, the water district's

00:01:00.474 --> 00:01:03.410
147 pumps stop too, with one to two hours

00:01:03.302 --> 00:01:03.926
of warning.

00:01:04.167 --> 00:01:05.954
An image in a feed is not a record you can

00:01:05.845 --> 00:01:06.555
check.

00:01:06.809 --> 00:01:09.608
Abiso reads every official notice once and

00:01:09.501 --> 00:01:10.812
turns it into an event.

00:01:10.946 --> 00:01:13.081
This is the live prototype on Cloud Run:

00:01:13.121 --> 00:01:17.039
341 disruption events from 204 official posts,

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:18.622
refreshed every three hours.

00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:23.203
Today in Basak, an MCWD water interruption

00:01:23.306 --> 00:01:25.493
for a mainline leak repair, with the link

00:01:25.375 --> 00:01:26.802
to the notice it came from.

00:01:27.055 --> 00:01:28.798
Most people here do not search.

00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:29.675
They ask.

00:01:29.587 --> 00:01:34.065
Naay water interruption sa Basak karon?

00:01:34.105 --> 00:01:36.017
The question goes to a Gemini agent built

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:38.403
with Google's Agent Development Kit, which

00:01:38.305 --> 00:01:40.587
hands it to a water specialist that can only

00:01:40.501 --> 00:01:41.855
read the stored notices.

00:01:42.243 --> 00:01:44.166
The answer comes back in Cebuano, with the

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:45.738
MCWD link.

00:01:46.073 --> 00:01:48.365
Here is the same question in the ADK developer

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:48.998
UI.

00:01:49.134 --> 00:01:50.772
Event two is the tool call:

00:01:50.959 --> 00:01:53.579
water, Basak, today's date.

00:01:54.052 --> 00:01:55.701
Event three is its result.

00:01:55.835 --> 00:01:57.400
Event four is the reply.

00:01:57.504 --> 00:01:59.458
The trace shows the coordinator hand off to

00:01:59.361 --> 00:02:01.706
the water agent, and the water agent call

00:02:01.609 --> 00:02:02.973
the water interruptions tool.

00:02:03.107 --> 00:02:04.715
No step answers from memory.

00:02:05.045 --> 00:02:06.441
The web page is a front.

00:02:06.513 --> 00:02:08.531
The real place is the family group chat.

00:02:08.634 --> 00:02:10.916
Ate Jen asks if there is still water.

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:14.156
Mama tags Abiso, and the reply is the live

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:16.066
answer from the same agent, with the same

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:16.478
link.

00:02:16.951 --> 00:02:18.578
Papa says fill the drum now.

00:02:18.966 --> 00:02:21.945
Then Kuya Migs forwards a MECO poster, and

00:02:21.837 --> 00:02:23.950
Abiso reads the image and answers with the

00:02:23.854 --> 00:02:25.005
event it compiled.

00:02:25.395 --> 00:02:26.515
The webhook is built;

00:02:26.503 --> 00:02:29.048
public access waits on Meta's app review.

00:02:30.505 --> 00:02:33.811
May pasok ba bukas sa Lapu-Lapu?

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:36.175
There is no official notice, so Abiso says

00:02:36.078 --> 00:02:37.009
exactly that.

00:02:37.113 --> 00:02:38.962
A wrong answer about classes is worse than

00:02:38.865 --> 00:02:39.816
no answer.

00:02:40.069 --> 00:02:41.233
Notices change.

00:02:41.473 --> 00:02:44.029
A MECO poster announces a line fault in Pajac

00:02:43.985 --> 00:02:44.853
Agora;

00:02:45.156 --> 00:02:47.195
the next day's poster says it is resolved.

00:02:47.499 --> 00:02:49.539
In Firestore that is one event with two source

00:02:49.431 --> 00:02:51.280
posts, not two events.

00:02:51.584 --> 00:02:53.697
Extensions and cancellations merge the same

00:02:53.589 --> 00:02:54.235
way.

00:02:54.487 --> 00:02:55.429
Under the hood.

00:02:55.902 --> 00:02:57.888
Every three hours Cloud Scheduler wakes the

00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:58.912
Cloud Run service.

00:02:59.047 --> 00:03:02.279
Gemini 3.8 Flash on Vertex AI compiles each

00:03:02.192 --> 00:03:04.558
new post once into a typed event:

00:03:05.136 --> 00:03:08.675
type, barangays, start, end, status, source.

00:03:09.253 --> 00:03:12.031
A reconciler merges extensions and cancellations;

00:03:12.039 --> 00:03:13.604
the events live in Firestore.

00:03:13.992 --> 00:03:15.535
Four doors read one store:

00:03:15.839 --> 00:03:18.701
the web page, the ask box agent, a calendar

00:03:18.625 --> 00:03:20.992
per barangay, the Messenger webhook.

00:03:21.232 --> 00:03:24.168
Other AI assistants call it through MCP and

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:25.002
A2A.

00:03:25.391 --> 00:03:26.744
One model call per notice;

00:03:26.879 --> 00:03:28.369
questions cost nothing.

00:03:28.624 --> 00:03:31.127
We measured it on fifty posts locked before

00:03:31.083 --> 00:03:32.331
any model saw them.

00:03:32.571 --> 00:03:34.832
Gemini got the type right every time, the

00:03:34.725 --> 00:03:36.574
start within an hour ninety two percent of

00:03:36.455 --> 00:03:38.875
the time, and barangays with ninety four percent

00:03:38.766 --> 00:03:39.507
overlap.

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:43.170
Status is the weakest field, and we say so.

00:03:43.424 --> 00:03:44.291
Abiso.

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:47.289
Official notices for Lapu-Lapu City, compiled

00:03:47.202 --> 00:03:49.325
once, answered where people already are.

00:03:49.630 --> 00:03:51.848
It is live now, and the code is public.

